---
import "../styles/site.css";
import Art from "../components/Art.astro";
import Blink from "../components/Blink.astro";
import Face from "../components/Face.astro";
import Head from "../components/Head.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Isles from "../components/Isles.astro";
import GitHubMark from "../components/GitHubMark.astro";
import { FILM_URL, siteLinks } from "../lib/links";
import { RELEASES_URL } from "../lib/github";
import { agentsLine, agentsToday, agentsTodayAnd } from "../lib/agents";

const { facts, dl, gh } = await siteLinks();
const title = "Ducter: say it once, hear back when it's done";
const description =
  `Ducter is an open-source personal AI on your own Mac or server. Tell one partner what you want. It hands the work to AI agents like ${agentsTodayAnd} and tells you when it's done.`;
const check = `<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3L13 4.5"/></svg>`;
const arrow = `<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8h10M9 4.5L12.5 8 9 11.5"/></svg>`;
const out = `<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12l8-8M6 4h6v6"/></svg>`;
const cross = `<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 4.5l7 7M11.5 4.5l-7 7"/></svg>`;
const lock = `<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 7V5a3 3 0 016 0v2h.5A1.5 1.5 0 0113 8.5v4a1.5 1.5 0 01-1.5 1.5h-7A1.5 1.5 0 013 12.5v-4A1.5 1.5 0 014.5 7H5zm1.6 0h2.8V5a1.4 1.4 0 00-2.8 0v2z"/></svg>`;
const ld = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
  name: "Ducter",
  applicationCategory: "DeveloperApplication",
  operatingSystem: "macOS, Linux, iOS, iPadOS",
  description,
  url: "https://ducter.ai",
  license: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0",
  offers: { "@type": "Offer", price: "0", priceCurrency: "USD" },
};
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<Head title={title} description={description} ld={ld} />
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

<Nav dl={dl} gh={gh} />

<main id="main">

<!-- ============ HERO: ack → job → result, playing itself ============ -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1>Say it once. <span class="line">Hear back when it's&nbsp;done.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">Ducter is a personal AI that runs on your own Mac or server. You tell <b>one partner</b> what you want. It hands the work to <b>the AI agents you already use</b>, on the plans you already pay for, and comes back when the work is done or a decision is yours to make.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn secondary lg" href="#how">See how it works</a>
        <a class="btn lg" href={dl.href}>{dl.label}</a>
      </div>
      <p class="cta-note">{dl.note}</p>
      <p class="facts">Free and open source under Apache 2.0. {agentsLine}</p>
      <ul class="platforms" aria-label="Where you use it">
        <li><Art name="laptop_awake" alt="" sizes="40px" />Mac</li>
        <li><Art name="server_awake" alt="" sizes="40px" />Linux server</li>
        <li><Art name="phone" alt="" sizes="24px" />iPhone and iPad</li>
        <li class="soon"><Art name="android" alt="" sizes="40px" />Android <small>coming soon</small></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="demo" id="demo" aria-label="A short example conversation with Ducter">
      <Face id="hero-face" faces={["idle", "working", "done"]} start="done" sizes="132px" eager />
      <div class="win">
        <div class="win-bar">
          <span class="avatar mascot" data-face="idle"><span class="clay"><Art class="f-idle" name="ducter_idle" alt="" sizes="52px" eager /><Blink sizes="52px" /></span></span>
          <div class="who"><b>Ducter</b><span class="presence" id="presence"><span>just finished something</span></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="convo">
          <div class="track" id="track">
            <div class="msg user step" data-step="user">Fix the flaky checkpoint test in <code>~/dev/hawdb</code>, then tell me.</div>
            <div class="msg ducter step" data-step="ack">I'll find out why <code>checkpoint_recovery</code> flakes, and fix it on its own branch.</div>
            <div class="step pop" data-step="chip"><span class="taskline" id="hero-chip" data-state="done"><span class="ic"><span class="i-work"><Fragment set:html={arrow} /></span><span class="i-done"><Fragment set:html={check} /></span></span><b>Fix CI</b><span class="st" id="hero-st"><span>· Done</span></span> ›</span></div>
            <div class="quiet step" data-step="quiet"><span class="clock"></span><span id="quiet-text">14 min later</span></div>
            <div class="msg ducter step" data-step="result">
              <p>CI is fixed. <code>checkpoint_recovery</code> slept a fixed 50&nbsp;ms for the flush, too short on a busy machine. It now waits for <code>wal.wait_durable(seq)</code>.</p>
              <div class="proof">
                <span class="mk"><Fragment set:html={check} />412 tests pass</span>
                <span class="mk"><Fragment set:html={check} />CI run #48219 · green</span>
                <span class="qlink">1 file changed ›</span>
                <span class="qlink">Fix CI ›</span>
              </div>
              <div class="proof"><span class="mk out"><Fragment set:html={out} />git push -u origin ducter/fix-ci</span></div>
              <div class="actions">
                <button class="btn secondary md" type="button" tabindex="-1">Open draft PR</button>
                <button class="btn md" type="button" tabindex="-1">Merge into main</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="composer" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="typed" id="typed" data-ph="Say something to Ducter…"></span>
          <span class="btn accent send" id="send"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10 16V4M4.5 9.5L10 4l5.5 5.5"/></svg></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo-ctl">
        <button class="textbtn sm" id="replay" type="button" hidden>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 8a5.5 5.5 0 109.6-3.6M12.5 1.8v2.8H9.7"/></svg>
          Play it again
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ ONLY WHEN IT MATTERS ============ -->
<section class="sec deep" id="how">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Silence means it's going fine.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">Tasks run in the background. You hear back when one is done, or when it needs you to decide something. Every decision comes with a suggested default.</p>
      <ul class="points">
        <li><span><b>Go, Hold or Reply…</b> Take the default, say "not yet", or answer in your own words.</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Or don't answer at all.</b> After 30 minutes it goes with the default, but only if that can be undone. Anything else waits for you.</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Done comes with proof:</b> what changed and how it checked.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="board-wrap" style="position:relative">
      <Face id="board-face" faces={["needsyou", "working", "done"]} start="working" sizes="118px" class="peek" />
      <div class="board" id="board" aria-label="On hand: every task at a glance">
        <div class="board-head"><b>On hand</b><small id="board-sum">3 working · 1 waiting</small></div>
        <div class="ask-slot" id="ask-slot">
          <div>
            <div class="ask" id="ask" role="group" aria-labelledby="ask-q">
              <div class="ask-top"><span id="ask-from">Port the runner to OAR 0.96 ›</span><span id="ask-time">30 min</span></div>
              <p class="q" id="ask-q">OAR 0.96 changed the steer API; 3 calls in the runner need to follow. Change them now?</p>
              <p class="def" id="ask-def">If you don't answer, I'll change them in 30 min. It can be undone.</p>
              <div class="bar"><i id="ask-bar"></i></div>
              <div class="actions">
                <button class="btn secondary md" type="button" id="ask-hold">Hold</button>
                <button class="btn md" type="button" id="ask-go">Change them</button>
                <span class="hint" id="ask-hint">Try it: press Change them</span>
              </div>
              <div class="resolved" id="ask-resolved"><Fragment set:html={check} /><span>Changing them now</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row" data-state="working" data-row="oar"><span class="glyph token"><Art name="coin_claude_code_plain" alt="" sizes="36px" /></span><span class="t"><b>Port the runner to OAR 0.96</b><span id="oar-st">Reading the changelog · Claude Code · cloud-1</span></span></div>
        <div class="row" data-state="working" data-row="prs"><span class="glyph token"><Art name="coin_codex_plain" alt="" sizes="36px" /></span><span class="t"><b>Review this week's 3 open PRs</b><span>Read 2; the third is waiting on CI · Codex · MacBook</span></span></div>
        <div class="row" data-state="waiting" data-row="notes"><span class="glyph bubble"><Art name="wait_ci" alt="" sizes="30px" /></span><span class="t"><b>Write the v0.4 release notes</b><span>Waiting for the v0.4 CI run · cloud-1</span></span></div>
        <div class="row" data-state="done" data-row="mem"><span class="glyph check"><Fragment set:html={check} /></span><span class="t"><b>Mem #8762 health check</b><span>Passed 3 times in a row; the issue can close · MacBook</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ YOUR COMPUTERS, YOUR PLANS ============ -->
<section class="sec" id="devices">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Your computers. Your plans.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Ducter lives on your Mac or on a server you own, and its tasks run on your computers, signed in to your AI agents with your own accounts. A coding task works in its own copy of your project, on its own branch, so your checkout stays as you left it. There's no Ducter account to make and no Ducter server in between.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stage-wrap reveal">
      <Isles />

      <div class="tray">
        <h3>You can also add</h3>
        <div class="stickers">
          <button class="sticker live" id="sticker-web" type="button" aria-describedby="web-detail"><Art name="ab_web" alt="" sizes="(min-width: 1040px) 96px, (min-width: 560px) 15vw, 19vw" /><b>Browse the web</b><small id="web-small">Drag onto this Mac, or tap</small></button>
          <div class="sticker lock"><Art name="ab_computer_later" alt="" sizes="(min-width: 1040px) 96px, (min-width: 560px) 15vw, 19vw" /><b>Use this computer</b><small>Coming later</small></div>
          <div class="sticker lock"><Art name="ab_phone_later" alt="" sizes="(min-width: 1040px) 96px, (min-width: 560px) 15vw, 19vw" /><b>Use a phone</b><small>Coming later</small></div>
          <div class="sticker lock"><Art name="ab_call_later" alt="" sizes="(min-width: 1040px) 96px, (min-width: 560px) 15vw, 19vw" /><b>Make calls</b><small>Coming later</small></div>
        </div>
        <div class="detail" id="web-detail">
          <h3>Browse the web</h3>
          <p>This Mac can look things up and read pages in Ducter's own Chrome window, apart from yours. Signing in, submitting forms and paying stay with you.</p>
          <button class="btn md" type="button" id="equip">Add to this Mac</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="points three">
      <li><span><b>Each task says where it runs.</b> Your partner picks the computer and the AI agent together, from what the task needs: your repo, a browser, a long run. One quiet line says where, and why if you tap it.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Lend it more computers.</b> A server keeps working while your Mac sleeps, and one switch lets your Mac do tasks for it. Closing your laptop? It moves what can move to a computer that stays on.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>It asks only when it matters:</b> when the right computer is asleep, or when a task would get more access, like your own Chrome. Between equal computers it just picks.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ PHONE ============ -->
<section class="sec deep" id="phone">
  <div class="wrap split flip">
    <div>
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>One thumb is enough.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">Your phone buzzes only when a decision is waiting for you, and never during your quiet hours. Answer it in one tap, or let the default happen and read about it in the morning.</p>
      <p class="body note">Quiet hours are 23:00 to 08:00 until you change them. With two decisions waiting, Go on all defaults answers both.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="phone-scene">
      <div class="phone" id="phone">
        <div class="screen">
          <div class="wall" aria-hidden="true">
            <i style="width:120%;aspect-ratio:1;left:-55%;top:52%;background:#ffb27a"></i>
            <i style="width:90%;aspect-ratio:1;right:-40%;top:-10%;background:#ffe9a8"></i>
            <i style="width:60%;aspect-ratio:1;right:-12%;bottom:-14%;background:#bfe0ff"></i>
          </div>
          <span class="island" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="clock" aria-hidden="true"><small>Monday, November 9</small><b>7:06</b></div>
          <div class="notif" id="notif" role="group" aria-label="A notification from Ducter">
            <div class="nh">
              <Art class="icon" name="ducter_idle" alt="" sizes="34px" />
              <div><b>Ducter</b><p id="notif-text">The rerun passes, but the branch is 23 commits behind main. Rebase before merging? Default: rebase, in 30 min.</p></div>
              <time>now</time>
            </div>
            <div class="nacts">
              <button class="btn secondary md" type="button" id="notif-hold">Hold</button>
              <button class="btn md" type="button" id="notif-go">Rebase</button>
            </div>
            <div class="done"><i><Fragment set:html={check} /></i><span id="notif-done">Rebasing. I'll tell you if CI doesn't pass.</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="thumb" id="thumb" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="home" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ WHERE YOU USE IT: Mac, server, iPhone and iPad, Android soon ============ -->
<section class="sec" id="where">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Wherever you are.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Ducter lives on one computer, your Mac or a server. Every other screen opens the same conversation: start a task at your desk, answer its question from your phone, read the result on your iPad.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="where">
      <li class="where-card reveal">
        <div class="where-art"><Art name="laptop_awake" alt="" sizes="160px" /></div>
        <h3>Mac</h3>
        <p>The desktop app, for Apple silicon. Ducter can live here and run tasks here, with its own Chrome window for the web.</p>
        <p class="where-state"><b>Ready</b><a href={dl.href}>{dl.href.startsWith("#") ? "Get it" : "Download"}</a></p>
      </li>
      <li class="where-card reveal">
        <div class="where-art"><Art name="server_awake" alt="" sizes="150px" /></div>
        <h3>A Linux server</h3>
        <p>x64 or arm64, at home or in the cloud. Your partner keeps working while your Mac sleeps, and your Mac can still do tasks for it.</p>
        <p class="where-state"><b>Ready</b><a href="/docs/install#a-linux-server-that-stays-on">Set one up</a></p>
      </li>
      <li class="where-card reveal">
        <div class="where-art"><Art name="phone" alt="" sizes="80px" /></div>
        <h3>iPhone and iPad</h3>
        <p>One app for both. On an iPad held across, On hand stands beside the conversation, and with a keyboard ⌘N starts a task.</p>
        <p class="where-state"><b>Public beta</b><a href="https://testflight.apple.com/join/Z4GvWt7t" rel="noopener">Join on TestFlight</a></p>
      </li>
      <li class="where-card soon reveal">
        <div class="where-art"><Art name="android" alt="" sizes="80px" /></div>
        <h3>Android</h3>
        <p>Today Ducter opens in your phone's browser, and you answer Go or Hold right from the notification.</p>
        <p class="where-state"><b>App coming soon</b><a href="/docs/phone">Use the browser</a></p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="body where-note">A phone or iPad needs an address it can reach from anywhere: Ducter on a server with your own domain. <a href="/docs/phone">Connect your phone</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ CONNECTED: memory, accounts, other AI agents ============ -->
<section class="sec deep" id="connected">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>It doesn't start from zero.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">Much of what your partner needs to know is somewhere else: in your mail, your calendar, and last week's sessions with your other AI tools. Your memory and your accounts work today; your other AI agents are next. None of it needs your passwords.</p>
      <ul class="points">
        <li><span><b>One memory for all your AIs.</b> <a href="https://mem.nowledge.co" rel="noopener">Nowledge Mem</a> keeps what you've decided and what you're working on, from every AI tool you connect to it. Your partner reads from it and adds to it, and you see Noted when it does; its tasks can use it too, under your partner's name. <span class="when">Works today, and optional: Mem is free to download, and without it your partner remembers your conversation.</span></span></li>
        <li><span><b>Your mail, calendar and other accounts.</b> If you use OOMOL's oo, it's one tap: your partner reads the accounts you already connected there. Otherwise paste an address and a key from <a href="https://github.com/oomol-lab/open-connector" rel="noopener">OpenConnector</a> (OOMOL's hosted one, or your own on your own computer or server). The AI agents never see your passwords. Reading is fine; anything that would send waits for your Go. <span class="when">Works today.</span></span></li>
        <li><span><b>Your AI agents, reaching each other.</b> With Nowledge Bridge, the Claude Code session in your terminal can hand your partner a job, and your partner can ask that session what it knows. It checks with you before it takes the job or sends the question. <span class="when">Early, and coming soon.</span></span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="memory-card reveal" aria-label="Example">
      <div class="msg user" style="align-self:end;justify-self:end">Rebase, never merge commits. Remember that for every repo.</div>
      <div class="msg ducter" style="margin-top:4px">Will do. From now on I'll rebase before merging, in every repo.
        <div class="noted"><i><Fragment set:html={check} /></i>Noted · Rebase before merging, every repo</div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiet" style="justify-self:center"><span class="clock"></span>9 days later</div>
      <div class="msg user" style="align-self:end;justify-self:end">Get the docs branch in <code>~/dev/hawdb</code> ready to merge.</div>
      <div class="msg ducter" style="margin-top:4px">It's rebased onto main, the way you like, and CI is green. It's ready for you to merge.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ HEADS-UP: restraint (D165, D173) ============ -->
<section class="sec" id="heads-up">
  <div class="wrap split flip">
    <div>
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>It looks out for you, quietly.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">Say yes once when you add your accounts, and your partner keeps an eye on your mail, calendar, GitHub and chat. It speaks up only when something needs you: one morning message with <b>at most three things</b>, and on a quiet day, nothing at all.</p>
      <ul class="points">
        <li><span><b>Each one comes with a next step.</b> Open the renewal page, look for somewhere to stay. Go does it, Hold leaves it, and How I know shows the mails behind it.</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Right away only when it can't wait</b>, and never in your quiet hours unless you asked for that kind.</span></li>
        <li><span><b>It never sends, replies, pays or deletes</b> on its own, and it doesn't tell you how much it read. Tap Useful, or Don't tell me this kind, and it learns.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="note-card reveal" aria-label="Example: a morning message">
      <div class="quiet" style="justify-self:center"><span class="clock"></span>08:00</div>
      <div class="msg ducter">Morning.</div>
      <div class="find">
        <p>ducter.dev expires on Nov 16, and it isn't renewed yet.</p>
        <div class="actions"><button class="btn md" type="button" tabindex="-1">Open the renewal page</button><button class="btn secondary md" type="button" tabindex="-1">Hold</button><span class="qlink">How I know ›</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="find">
        <p>You land in Tokyo on Nov 21, and nothing is booked for that night.</p>
        <div class="actions"><button class="btn md" type="button" tabindex="-1">Find a place to stay</button><button class="btn secondary md" type="button" tabindex="-1">Hold</button><span class="qlink">How I know ›</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ TRUST ============ -->
<section class="sec ink-band" id="trust">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>It asks before anything reaches other people.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">A task doesn't stop you for every command. Emails, posts, PR comments and pushes to shared branches wait for your Go, and every one is written down. In a folder that isn't a git repo, every change can be undone with one tap. A few things it never does at all.</p>
      <ul class="nevers">
        <li><b>It never merges into main.</b><span>A finished task offers Merge into main or Open draft PR, and waits for you.</span></li>
        <li><b>It never types your passwords.</b><span>You sign in yourself, in its browser window. The AI never sees what you type.</span></li>
        <li><b>It never pays.</b><span>Payments are always left to you.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="ledger reveal" id="ledger">
      <div class="ledger-head"><b>Sent out today</b><small>Monday</small></div>
      <ol>
        <li class="step"><code>git push -u origin ducter/fix-ci</code><span class="verdict ran"><Fragment set:html={check} />Ran: its own branch</span></li>
        <li class="step"><code>gh pr create --draft "Fix flaky checkpoint_recovery"</code><span class="verdict asked"><Fragment set:html={check} />Asked you; you said Go</span></li>
        <li class="step"><code>git push origin main</code><span class="verdict waits"><Fragment set:html={lock} />Waits for you, always</span></li>
        <li class="step"><code>email: load-test numbers → a HawDB contributor</code><span class="verdict asked"><Fragment set:html={out} />Asks you first</span></li>
        <li class="step"><code>sign in to github.com</code><span class="verdict yours"><Fragment set:html={lock} />Yours to do</span></li>
        <li class="step"><code>pay: renew a domain</code><span class="verdict yours"><Fragment set:html={lock} />Never Ducter's call</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ DEPTH ============ -->
<section class="sec" id="depth">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Open anything. Any time.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Most days you stay in the conversation. When you want a closer look, <b>On hand</b> shows every task at a glance. Open one to read what it did, step by step, and the diff of every file it changed. You can write to it directly while it works.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="task-win reveal" aria-label="An opened task">
      <div class="tw-bar">
        <span class="crumbs"><span>Conversation</span><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>On hand</span><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><b>Fix CI · #1592</b></span>
      </div>
      <div class="tw-page">
        <div class="tw-head">
          <Face id="task-face" faces={["done"]} start="done" sizes="116px" />
          <div>
            <div class="standing"><b>Done</b><span>· started 14 min ago</span></div>
            <p class="outcome">The flaky checkpoint test is fixed.</p>
            <p class="said">Rebased; all 412 tests pass and CI is green. The cause was a fixed 50&nbsp;ms sleep in the test, now a wait for durability.</p>
            <div class="proof">
              <span class="mk"><Fragment set:html={check} />20 local reruns</span>
              <span class="mk"><Fragment set:html={check} />CI run #48219 · green</span>
              <span class="qlink">1 file changed ›</span>
            </div>
            <div class="proof"><span class="mk out"><Fragment set:html={out} />git push -u origin ducter/fix-ci</span></div>
            <div class="actions"><button class="btn secondary md" type="button" tabindex="-1">Open draft PR</button><button class="btn md" type="button" tabindex="-1">Merge into main</button></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="tw-h">What it did</h3>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li class="said-small"><small>What Ducter asked for</small>Find out why HawDB #1592's CI fails, and fix it.</li>
          <li class="fold">› Ran 3 commands</li>
          <li>All three failures are in <code>checkpoint_recovery</code>: it sleeps a fixed 50&nbsp;ms for the flush.</li>
          <li class="fold">› Edited 1 file</li>
          <li class="note">Progress saved · Confirmed flaky; wait for durability</li>
          <li class="said-small"><small>Told Ducter · needs you to decide</small>The rerun passes. But the branch is 23 commits behind main: rebase before merging?</li>
          <li class="fold">› Ran 3 commands</li>
