<!-- ============ OPEN ============ -->
<section class="sec deep" id="open">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Yours to read and run.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="cards3">
      <div class="card reveal"><div class="card-art"><Art name="ducter_working" alt="" sizes="120px" /></div><h3>Open source</h3><p>Apache 2.0. Every prompt Ducter writes and every line of code that touches your work is in the source.</p></div>
      <div class="card reveal"><div class="card-art"><Art name="server_awake" alt="" sizes="140px" /></div><h3>Self-hosted</h3><p>Your Mac, or a Linux server you own. Your conversation and tasks stay in one folder there that only your account can read.</p></div>
      <div class="card reveal"><div class="card-art coins"><Art name="coin_claude_code" alt="" sizes="64px" /><Art name="coin_codex" alt="" sizes="64px" /><Art name="coin_pi" alt="" sizes="64px" /><Art name="coin_deepseek_harness" alt="" sizes="64px" /></div><h3>No lock-in</h3><p>Ducter works through each AI agent's own app, signed in as you, on your existing plan. Use whichever one you have, and switch for any task.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="under reveal" id="under">
      <div>
        <h3>Built on the agents you have</h3>
        <p class="body">For people who already run several AI agents at once: what Ducter does so they hold up as one partner.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="points">
        <li><span><b>One adapter, four agents.</b> Claude Code, Codex, pi and DeepSeek Harness, started through <a href="https://github.com/botiverse/oar" rel="noopener">OAR</a> in clean sessions that still carry your own skills and settings.</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Small windows on purpose.</b> Your partner and its tasks work in about 200K tokens. A long conversation stays coherent through short digests and recall, not by replaying everything.</span></li>
        <li><span><b>The facts about each agent, in one place.</b> Context windows, compaction points and versions are checked against the real programs, and <code>ducter doctor</code> warns when yours is outside what was checked.</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Each agent's own browser first.</b> Ducter's own Chrome is the fallback, on your Mac or your server.</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Keys stay out of tasks.</b> A key or token you paste is taken out of what a task is told, and hidden everywhere Ducter shows one.</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Budgets are tests.</b> Every prompt and tool list has a size limit that fails the build, and updates are rehearsed end to end on a Linux VM before a release.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="install" id="install">
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:28px">Get Ducter</h3>
        <p class="body" style="margin-top:10px">You need {agentsToday} installed and signed in on the computer that does the work. Ducter checks everything else and tells you the one thing to fix, if there is one.</p>
        {!facts.isPublic && <p class="body" style="margin-top:10px">The repository opens to the public soon. Until then, these are the exact steps it will take.</p>}
      </div>
      <div class="panel-box">
        <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Ways to install">
          <button role="tab" id="tab-mac" aria-controls="p-mac" aria-selected="true">Mac app</button>
          <button role="tab" id="tab-cli" aria-controls="p-cli" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Command line</button>
          <button role="tab" id="tab-srv" aria-controls="p-srv" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Server</button>
          <button role="tab" id="tab-ios" aria-controls="p-ios" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">iPhone and iPad</button>
          <button role="tab" id="tab-agent" aria-controls="p-agent" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Your AI agent</button>
        </div>
        <div class="panel" id="p-mac" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-mac" style="margin-top:14px">
          <p>Paste this into Terminal. It downloads the signed app, checks it, puts it in Applications and opens it:</p>
          <div class="term"><button class="btn sm copy" type="button" data-copy="curl -fsSL https://ducter.ai/install.sh | sh">Copy</button><pre><span class="p">$ </span>curl -fsSL https://ducter.ai/install.sh | sh</pre></div>
          <p>Ducter checks your Mac, then opens the conversation. Closing the window doesn't stop it. It needs a Mac with Apple silicon.</p>
          <p>Or <a href={facts.dmgUrl ?? RELEASES_URL}>download the .dmg</a> and drag Ducter to Applications, or <a href="/docs/install#build-it-from-the-source-instead">build it from the source</a>. On iPhone and iPad: <a href="https://testflight.apple.com/join/Z4GvWt7t" rel="noopener">join the beta</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel" id="p-cli" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-cli" style="margin-top:14px" hidden>
          <p>The same line installs the <code>ducter</code> command in <code>~/.local/bin</code>. On a Mac it comes with the app; on Linux it's the <code>ducter</code> bundle:</p>
          <div class="term"><button class="btn sm copy" type="button" data-copy="curl -fsSL https://ducter.ai/install.sh | sh">Copy</button><pre><span class="p">$ </span>curl -fsSL https://ducter.ai/install.sh | sh</pre></div>
          <p>Then check this computer, and start your partner (on a Mac, the app opens too):</p>
          <div class="term"><button class="btn sm copy" type="button" data-copy="ducter doctor&#10;ducter up">Copy</button><pre><span class="c"># every missing piece comes with its fix</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>ducter doctor
<span class="c"># starts your partner</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>ducter up</pre></div>
          <p><code>ducter status</code> shows your tasks and the decisions waiting for you. Or <a href="/docs/install#the-ducter-command">build it from the source</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel" id="p-srv" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-srv" style="margin-top:14px" hidden>
          <div class="term"><button class="btn sm copy" type="button" data-copy="curl -fsSL https://ducter.ai/install.sh | sh -s -- --service&#10;ducter domain ducter.example.com">Copy</button><pre><span class="c"># on the server (x64 or arm64 Linux): runs as a service</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>curl -fsSL https://ducter.ai/install.sh | sh -s -- --service
<span class="c"># point an A record at the server, then: HTTPS, and a code for your Mac and phone</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>ducter domain ducter.example.com</pre></div>
          <p>Your partner keeps working while your Mac sleeps. It only listens on the server itself (127.0.0.1); <code>ducter domain</code> checks your DNS, sets up HTTPS with Caddy and gives you a code. No domain? An SSH tunnel works for your Mac.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel" id="p-ios" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-ios" style="margin-top:14px" hidden>
          <p>One app for iPhone and iPad, in public beta through Apple's TestFlight. It connects to Ducter on your server with the address and code from <code>ducter pair</code>.</p>
          <p><a class="btn" href="https://testflight.apple.com/join/Z4GvWt7t" rel="noopener">Join the beta</a></p>
          <p>On Android, or any phone, open the same address in the browser; the Android app is coming soon. <a href="/docs/phone">Your phone</a> has the details.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel" id="p-agent" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-agent" style="margin-top:14px" hidden>
          <p>Let Claude Code, Codex or another agent set Ducter up for you. Ask it:</p>
          <div class="term"><button class="btn sm copy" type="button" data-copy="Install the ducter-deploy skill from github.com/wey-gu/ducter/tree/main/skills and deploy Ducter on my server.">Copy</button><pre>Install the ducter-deploy skill from github.com/wey-gu/ducter/tree/main/skills and deploy Ducter on my server.</pre></div>
          <p>The skills are also at <code>https://ducter.ai/skills/ducter-deploy/SKILL.md</code> (and <code>ducter-operate</code>, <code>ducter-troubleshoot</code>). <a href="/docs/for-agents">For AI agents</a> says what they do.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="final" id="final">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Face id="final-face" faces={["napping", "idle"]} start="napping" sizes="168px" />
